JPA (Jakarta Persistence API)
----------------------------
JPA stands for Jakarta Persistence API.
It is a specification (set of rules/guidelines), not an implementation.
Similar to an interface, it only defines what should be done, not how it should be done.
 

JPA provides:
-----------
Annotations (@Entity, @Table, @Id, etc.)
Interfaces (EntityManager, Entity Transaction, etc.)
Rules for ORM (Object Relational Mapping)
JPA defines these annotations but does not provide the actual logic.

Hibernate
---------
Hibernate is an ORM Framework.
Hibernate is an implementation of JPA.
It provides the actual logic for all JPA operations.

Responsible for:
--------------
Saving objects into the database
Updating records
Deleting records
Fetching records
Generating SQL queries

