CASCADE TYPES
CascadeType.ALL      -> Persist, Merge, Remove, Refresh, Detach
CascadeType.PERSIST  -> Save child automatically
CascadeType.MERGE    -> Update child automatically
CascadeType.REMOVE   -> Delete child automatically
CascadeType.REFRESH  -> Reload child
CascadeType.DETACH   -> Detach child
====================================================

FETCH TYPES
FetchType.EAGER -> Load parent and child immediately.

FetchType.LAZY  -> Load child only when required.(Default for collections.)
====================================================

LEGEND
--------
PK = Primary Key

FK = Foreign Key

@JoinColumn = Creates Foreign Key

mappedBy = Inverse side (does not own FK)

Owning Side = Contains Foreign Key

@JoinTable = Creates Junction Table

@MapsId = Shared Primary Key
====================================================

IMPORTANT NOTES
---------------
1. Owning side always contains the Foreign Key.

2. mappedBy is used only on the inverse side.

3. @JoinTable is used in Many-to-Many mappings.

4. One-to-One can use a Foreign Key or Shared Primary Key.

5. One-to-Many usually stores the Foreign Key in the "Many" table.

6. Many-to-One always contains the Foreign Key.

7. Default Fetch:
   - @ManyToOne = EAGER
   - @OneToOne = EAGER
   - @OneToMany = LAZY
   - @ManyToMany = LAZY

8. Cascade is optional and depends on the business requirement.



